# inner: try { throw A; } catch (...) { throw; } where the rethrow is call site 2, whose
# landing pad (index 1) is the catch block's cleanup: end_catch, then resume. The
# rethrown exception is the same one: main catches A with the same object, and after
# main's end_catch no exception is left.
title: rethrow from a catch-all handler reaches the outer handler with the same exception
ref: libsupc++ eh_throw.cc (__cxa_rethrow), eh_catch.cc (__cxa_end_catch of a rethrown exception); ADR 0020

